WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
If you have tried direct pressure and wound packing, but the bleeding on an arm or leg just won't stop,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.200
it is potentially life-threatening situation.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.900
In this case, for anyone age 2 and older, we need to move quickly to apply a tourniquet.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:19.000
For children under the age of 2, remember to continue using direct pressure instead.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.900
Your instructor will demonstrate and pass out tourniquets so you can practice together.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.600
To apply a tourniquet, first place the tourniquet 2 to 3 inches above the wound,

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.299
making sure you aren't placing it directly over a joint, like an elbow or knee.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:36.700
Pull the strap as tight as you possibly can and secure it.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.700
Then, you'll turn the windlass, that's the stick-like rod on the device, until the bleeding completely stops.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.500
Once it's secure, your final step is to record the exact time you put it on.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.200
This is vital information for the surgeons who will treat the person later.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.500
Most importantly, once that tourniquet is on, do not take it off for any reason.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.400
Only a doctor in a hospital should do that.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:04.099
For our practice today, I want you to apply the tourniquet to your own arm or leg.

00:01:04.099 --> 00:01:06.900
You don't need to tighten it to the point of stopping blood flow,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.400
but I want you to tighten the strap until you feel firm pressure,

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.699
and then give the windlass a few turns until you feel that pressure increase.

00:01:14.699 --> 00:01:17.000
Once you felt how the mechanism works,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.599
you can take it off and go ahead and dispose of your used gauze squares and rolls.

00:01:21.699 --> 00:01:27.699
Finally, removing your gloves in the proper manner helps to keep ourselves safe from contamination.

00:01:27.699 --> 00:01:32.699
Using your dominant hand, pinch the outside of the opposite glove near the wrist,

00:01:32.699 --> 00:01:34.900
being careful not to touch your skin,

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.900
and peel it downward so it turns inside out as it comes off.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.400
Hold that crumpled glove in your still-gloved hand.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:47.199
Now, slide the fingers of your clean hand under the wrist cuff of the remaining glove

00:01:47.199 --> 00:01:49.400
and peel it off over the first one.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.699
This should leave both gloves inside out and nested together.

00:01:52.699 --> 00:01:55.099
Drop them straight into the biohazard container

00:01:55.099 --> 00:01:59.099
and immediately wash your hands with soap and water for at least 30 seconds.

